# AI Content Monetization — environment configuration example
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in as needed. Values here are safe placeholders.
# The CDK deploy sources most configuration from `cdk.json` (context.iab); this
# file documents the runtime overrides a deployer may set.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS allowed origins (TM-02, security-hardening-phase2)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend echoes Access-Control-Allow-Origin from a configured allow-list,
# never a wildcard "*". It is resolved at runtime in this order of precedence:
#   1. ALLOWED_ORIGINS (this var, comma-separated) — explicit, highest precedence.
#   2. SSM parameter /cm/ui/origin — written by the UI stack (CMUIStack) on deploy
#      with the deployed CloudFront portal origin, read by the backend at invoke time.
#
# Leave ALLOWED_ORIGINS BLANK for a demo deploy: the portal origin is resolved
# automatically from the deployed CloudFront distribution via SSM /cm/ui/origin,
# so no manual value is needed.
#
# For PRODUCTION, set it to your portal's custom domain(s), e.g.:
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://portal.publisher.com
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://portal.publisher.com,https://admin.publisher.com
#
# For LOCAL UI DEVELOPMENT against the DEPLOYED backend, add your Vite dev origin
# so the browser's credentialed cross-origin requests are not blocked. The Vite
# dev server runs on http://localhost:3000 (source/ui/vite.config.ts):
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# (The dev CDK deploy already includes http://localhost:3000 via cdk.json
# context.iab.allowedOrigins; set this var to override per-deployer. Production
# deploys MUST NOT include localhost.)
#
# If neither ALLOWED_ORIGINS nor /cm/ui/origin resolves, the backend omits the
# credentialed CORS headers (fail-safe) rather than emitting "*".
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
